From d353978fb998d7e953ee6347fc86966ea132aa05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 02:30:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: sun50i-a64: Fix USB PHY phy_ctrl
 register range

phy_ctrl is declared as 0x14 bytes, but sun50i_a64_cfg sets
phy0_dual_route, so sun4i_usb_phy0_reroute() reads and writes
REG_PHY_OTGCTL at offset 0x20 -- past the end of the declared resource.
It only works because ioremap() rounds the mapping up to a page.

Declare 0x100, matching A100, D1 and A523. Nothing else claims that
range, and the highest offset the driver ever touches from this base is
0x20. The PHY_* constants used with sun4i_usb_phy_write() are internal
PHY register indices shifted into the phyctl word, not MMIO offsets.
Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64.dtsi
index 2b2df70c109b..2c879e87e51f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64.dtsi
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@ usb_otg: usb@1c19000 {
 
 		usbphy: phy@1c19400 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy";
-			reg = <0x01c19400 0x14>,
+			reg = <0x01c19400 0x100>,
 			      <0x01c1a800 0x4>,
 			      <0x01c1b800 0x4>;
 			reg-names = "phy_ctrl",
-- 
2.43.0

